  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/92B014">Definition <span data-tag="92B014">6.4.1.1</span>.</a>$n$-topos Let $0 \leq n < \infty $. An $\infty $-category $\calX $ is an <em>$n$-topos</em> if there exists a small $\infty $-category $\calC $ and an (accessible) left exact localization </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  L: \calP _{\leq n-1}(\calC ) \rightarrow \calX , \]
</div>
  <p> where $\calP _{\leq n-1}(\calC )$ denotes the full subcategory of $\calP (\calC )$ spanned by the $(n-1)$-truncated objects.Pcalleq@$\calP _{\leq n}(\calC )$ </p>
